      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-3781",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "First, note that the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n, \\qquad\\qquad 2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} = \\dfrac{7\\pi}{4} + 2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nSolving the two equations above for $x,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{7\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ 2x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & 2x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x=-\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\pi n, & \\, & \\, & x=\\frac{5\\pi }{8}+\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979131/example-3781.json",
          "file_sha256": "49ea9e34ac6899664730aa1d64725feeb7cd49b926d3c37276060b3a55326658"
